<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<chapter xml:id="ch19-conservation-laws" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Conservation Laws and the Language of Fields</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>Using the boundary theorems of Chapter 18, we translate conservation of a stored quantity into a local equation for density, flux, and sources. Time-dependent fields use the same partial derivatives and chain rules as earlier chapters. Each physical model supplies its own flux or force law; the additional formulas needed for heat, waves, potentials, and Maxwell equations are introduced here.</p>
  </introduction>

